@startuml neural-cache
' EmbeddingCache internals: a lock-free DashMap for the payload, a mutex-guarded VecDeque
' for LRU recency. Shows precisely where a lock IS and IS NOT taken, and the two costs.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/neural-cache.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/components/neural/cache.md §3.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title EmbeddingCache — lock-free payload, mutex-guarded recency

rectangle "**Caller** (any thread)\nembedder.embed(text)" as caller #2E7D32

rectangle "**hash_text**\nutil::hash::safe_hash\n≥ 16 B ⟶ gxhash64\n< 16 B ⟶ xxh3_64" as hash #00838F

rectangle "**entries**\nDashMap<u64, Arc<[f32]>>\n**lock-free** sharded probe\nhit ⟹ Arc::clone (no copy)" as map #00838F

rectangle "**access_order**\nparking_lot::Mutex<VecDeque<u64>>\n⚠ **the only lock**" as order #00838F

rectangle "**Encoder**\nModernBertModel forward pass\n≈ 10⁶ × the cost of a probe" as model #2E7D32

caller --> hash : text
hash --> map : 64-bit key
map --> caller : **hit** — Arc<[f32]>
map --> model : **miss**
model --> map : insert(key, Arc<[f32]>)

map ..> order : get: touch (move key to back)
map ..> order : insert: evict front if full,\nthen push key to back

note right of order #FFEBEE
  **Cost of the touch.** `order.iter().position(…)`
  is a linear scan of up to max_entries keys, and it
  runs **while holding the mutex** — on both get and
  insert. The map probe is 𝒪(1) and lock-free; the
  recency update is 𝒪(N) and serialized. With 10 000
  entries and many threads this is the contention
  point, not DashMap. It is still ≈ 10⁻⁶ of a forward
  pass, so it never dominates a //miss// — only a
  hit-heavy, highly-parallel workload feels it.
end note

note bottom of map #E0F2F1
  **Digest-only keying.** The text is not stored, only its
  64-bit digest. Two distinct texts that collide return the
  //wrong// vector. At N = 10 000 entries the birthday bound
  gives ≈ N²/2⁶⁵ ≈ 2.7 × 10⁻¹² — negligible, but it is a
  correctness trade, not an impossibility.
end note

@enduml
